CaveWii -- third-party component notices
=========================================

This file lists the third-party source/library components vendored under
third_party/ and source/*, or linked at build time, and the runtime assets
under assets/ that carry a license other than this project's own, with the
verified license, upstream URL, and copyright holder for each. Full license
TEXT for every entry below ships alongside this file under
LICENSES/<name>.txt -- this file summarizes and points to that text; the
LICENSES/ file is authoritative for the exact terms.

Runtime/binary assets (textures, sounds) shipped under assets/ have their
own licenses, documented in assets/README.md (shipped alongside this file
in the release) -- that file, not this one, is authoritative for asset
credits and covers CC0/CC-BY grants per file. The bundled default textures
are Earth & Ash, original art dedicated under CC0 1.0 (listed with hashes in
assets/earth-and-ash-manifest.json; licence text assets/CC0-1.0.txt). Two
asset entries are worth calling out here specifically: one asset carrying a
copyleft license, and the optional Isabella II texture pack, whose CC BY 3.0
license requires attribution:

- The Wii hand pointer: assets/pointer.png and packs/beta-base/pointer.png
  We did not make this pointer; we use it unchanged, with thanks.
  Author: the Homebrew Channel team (Team Twiizers / fail0verflow).
  License: GNU General Public License v2 (GPLv2).
  Origin: Homebrew Channel, https://github.com/fail0verflow/hbc/tree/master/channel/channelapp/data
  (per https://wiibrew.org/wiki/Homebrew_Channel). Kept as-is (known
  license). Since 2026-10-27 (maintainer decision) it is the pointer for
  every texture pack, including the default; the Earth & Ash arrow is no
  longer used.
  License file: LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt

- Controller button glyphs (cells 0-31 of assets/gui/approved-controls.png
  and of the fallback atlas assets/controls.png)
  We did not make these; we use them, with credit.
  Authors: the WiiBrew uploaders Clorox, Hiker13526, Flark and Crayon (2008),
  from WiiBrew's Category:Controller_Buttons,
  https://wiibrew.org/wiki/Category:Controller_Buttons
  No licence is stated on wiibrew.org. Used with credit by the maintainer's
  2026-10-22 decision. Cells 32-41 of approved-controls.png and the other
  cells of controls.png are original CaveWii art, CC0 1.0.
  In approved-controls.png, 26 of cells 0-31 are WiiBrew art. Cells 14, 15,
  22 and 23 (the Classic Controller L, R, ZL and ZR keycaps) are blank
  keycaps drawn by the CaveWii project (2026-10-31, GPL-3.0-or-later); the
  game draws their letters with the active pack font.
  Cells 44-49 of approved-controls.png (PC keyboard and mouse: a blank 1u
  key, a blank wide key over cells 45-46, and the left, right and wheel
  mouse buttons) are drawn by the CaveWii project (2026-10-31,
  GPL-3.0-or-later); the game draws key names with the active pack font.

- CavEX / fCavEX, the upstream engine this project builds on
  We did not write the original engine; we build on it.
  Authors: xtreme8000 (CavEX, Copyright (c) 2022 ByteBit/xtreme8000), with
  further fork work by yyy257, ByteBit and jilleb (named in meta.xml).
  Licence: GNU General Public License v3 (GPLv3).
  Origin: https://github.com/xtreme8000/CavEX
  This covers resources/vertex.shader and resources/fragment.shader
  (xtreme8000) and the original parts of source/. CaveWii changes are under
  the same licence.

- Original CaveWii artwork that is GPL, not CC0
  icon.png (the new CAVEX logo, project-own art, maintainer 2026-10-30),
  assets/sound/menu/*.wav (nine menu cues, synthesised in-project, no
  recordings from other games), assets/gui/title-logo.png and
  assets/gui/reception.png (rasterised from the committed original Earth
  SVG), assets/gui/controller-pictures.png (controller drawings, made by the
  original CaveWii team art, maintainer-approved 2026-10-28;
  not Nintendo artwork). Original CaveWii artwork, GPL-3.0-or-later, same as
  the code. They are not CC0.

- Colormaps and menu backdrop
  assets/misc/grasscolor.png and assets/misc/foliagecolor.png: CaveWii
  generated colormaps (tools/gen_cc0_colormaps.py); the earlier files had an
  untraceable origin and were replaced. CC0 1.0.
  assets/gui/menu-background.png: in-game render of CaveWii's own world
  generator (seed 42, fixed camera, bundled Earth & Ash textures), cropped and
  nearest-neighbour scaled to 1024x576. CC0 1.0. Provenance:
  assets/gui/menu-background.provenance.json.

- Optional texture pack: "Isabella II" by Bonemouse
  License: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported (CC BY 3.0 Unported),
  http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
  Forum thread: http://www.minecraftforum.net/topic/242175-Isabella/
  Textures by Bonemouse. Files derived from Isabella II (some of them
  modified for CaveWii_v2) ship ONLY in the optional pack folder
  texturepacks/isabella-ii/ (a pick-able, partial pack -- source
  packs/isabella-ii/ in the repository; files it lacks fall back to the
  Earth & Ash default in assets/; no Isabella II file is in assets/):
  terrain.png, particles.png, gui/items.png, terrain/sun.png,
  terrain/moon.png, environment/clouds.png, gui/crafting.png,
  gui/furnace.png, gui/gui.png, gui/icons.png and gui/inventory.png, plus
  anim.png (adapted 2026-10-11: Beta 1.7.3 animation motion recoloured with
  Isabella II tile colours, with Isabella II's own ice tile). The same
  folder's pointer.png and font/default.png are NOT Isabella II files: they
  are original CaveWii artwork dedicated under CC0 1.0 (2026-10-11,
  artwork/isabella-ii-extras/make_pointer_font.py).
  The pack's own "About Isabella.txt" ships UNEDITED (as its licence
  requires) in LICENSES/Isabella-II/About Isabella.txt and in
  texturepacks/isabella-ii/About Isabella.txt.
  License file: LICENSES/Isabella-II/LICENSE.txt (also
  texturepacks/isabella-ii/LICENSE.txt)
  Also modified/derived from Isabella II (CC BY 3.0, Bonemouse):
  packs/isabella-ii/gui/menu-background.png (shipped as
  texturepacks/isabella-ii/gui/menu-background.png): in-game render of
  CaveWii terrain drawn with Isabella II textures, cropped and scaled to
  1024x576. packs/isabella-ii/mob/char.png (shipped as
  texturepacks/isabella-ii/mob/char.png): original CaveWii/Astra 64x32 player
  skin adapted to Isabella II's palette and shading; Isabella II by Bonemouse,
  CC BY 3.0 (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/,
  http://www.minecraftforum.net/topic/242175-Isabella/). Not Bonemouse's
  original skin.

- Boot credit cards (assets/gui/startup-credits/)
  BagHeads boot-card artwork (assets/gui/startup-credits/*) (c) 2026 BagHeads.
  Licensed CC BY-ND 4.0: redistribute freely with this game, including format
  conversion and atlas packing; no derivative artwork. The BagHeads name and
  card identify the original publisher of CaveWii; forks must remove or replace
  them and may not present modified builds as BagHeads releases. Provenance: AI
  style transfer from an original image by the maintainer, then hand-edited
  into a 6-frame animation.
  Card text uses the bundled CC0 Earth & Ash bitmap font
  (assets/font/default.png). The "Built on" card credits CavEX by xtreme8000
  and fCavEX by yyy257, ByteBit and jilleb; it states that CaveWii is not
  affiliated with Mojang or Nintendo. credits.txt and build_atlas.py in that
  folder are project text/code (GPL-3.0-or-later).

